---
title: Page not found — FrontierJS Supply Co.
render: static
---
<!--
  The 404 page, and it is a ROUTE like any other so it goes through the layout
  and looks like the site.

  `trailingSlash: 'always'` emits it at `404/index.html` rather than the
  `404.html` most static hosts look for by name, so `deploy/serve.js` names the
  path. A host that wants the conventional name gets a copy in a postbuild step;
  what must not happen is a 404 page served with a 200, which is a dead link a
  crawler indexes as a real page.
-->
<div class="container stack">
  <h1>That page has moved on</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">
    The link may be old, or the product may have been retired — a retired
    product loses its page, deliberately.
  </p>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/catalog/">Browse the catalogue</a></p>
</div>
